-- 662_location_linear_spot_repair.sql — cast location spots built around a feature that runs AWAY from the viewer
-- (a winding creek, a river snaking through a valley, a canal receding, a tunnel of branches or torii) get a spot at
-- its side instead, same place (2026-10-02, NIGHTLY_COMPOSITION_AUDIT_PLAN.md follow-up to 661).
--
-- Why: 661 only looked for route nouns. Its post-apply live check drew "a redwood stand reflected in a still tannic
-- creek winding through the grove" and the render was the person centred on the creek, receding behind: the same
-- corridor shot with no route word. scripts/fix-location-route-spots.js --linear prefilters on the running-away words
-- (104 cast spots), the judge flagged 58, three tunnels it passed were added by hand (sottoportego passageways, the
-- Colosseum hypogeum tunnels, dwarven mining tunnels), every rewrite read, 8 edited by hand.
-- Render test on Kevin's account before any row changed (real nightly-dreams via force_slot_input, same template, 12
-- spots x 2, original vs rewrite): route-staged 18/24 -> 4/24 by the vision tag, swaps 24/24 both arms, identity mean
-- 0.70 vs 0.67 (all >= 0.59 but one small-figure Fushimi render at 0.47).
-- NOT applied: Times Square "canyon of LED billboards" (2/2 route-staged both arms: the place IS the canyon) and
-- "candy-striped trunks stretching skyward" (vertical, not a corridor).
-- Shared postcard spots are split as in 661 (original row postcard-only, a new cast-only row carries the rewrite: 48);
-- cast-only spots are rewritten in place (11). Every statement is guarded, so a re-run changes nothing.
-- ROLLBACK (the tool's --rollback writes it): DELETE each cast-only twin (location_key + new text,
-- pure_scene_eligible = false) and set its original row's character_eligible back to true; in-place = swap SET/WHERE.

